> I know that they are a consortium of various vendors.

Unfortunately you don't know that as it isn't true. The Open Software
Foundation is an international, not-for-profit research and software
development organization with a membership made up of systems vendors,
software suppliers, end users and academic and research organizations.

OSF is a source technology supplier. Certain techology is available to
anyone wishing to license it (eg OSF/1, Motif) others are only available
to members (eg OSF/1 MK, ANDF, DME) until is becomes officially released.

For membership information you should contact:

